+    <section class="journal" id="journal">
+      <h2>Roaster's Journal</h2>
+      <div class="journal-text" id="journal-text">
+        <p>Every bag we roast begins months before it reaches our shop, usually at a long wooden table in the
+          highlands of Colombia, Ethiopia, or Guatemala. Twice a year our head roaster travels to meet the
+          farmers we work with, sitting down to cup dozens of small lots side by side. We taste for sweetness,
+          clarity, and balance, and we take notes on which farms are experimenting with new fermentation methods
+          or shade-grown varieties.</p>
+        <p>We buy directly from cooperatives and family farms whenever we can, and we pay well above the
+          fair-trade minimum. Prices are agreed before the harvest, so growers can invest in their land and
+          their workers without worrying about swings in the commodity market. Many of our relationships are
+          now more than a decade old, and a few of the farms we visited as strangers now send us photos of
+          their children each Christmas.</p>
+        <p>Once a lot is chosen, we request pre-shipment samples from the mill to make sure the green coffee
+          that arrives matches what we tasted at origin. Back home, each delivery is rested, sample-roasted,
+          and cupped again before it earns a place on our menu. If a coffee does not meet the bar, we send
+          it back or pass on it, even when that leaves a gap in our lineup.</p>
+        <p>Sustainability shapes every step. We favor farms that protect watersheds and native tree cover,
+          and we ship our green coffee in reusable jute sacks that local artists and gardeners collect from
+          us. Our roasting happens in small batches, never more than a few days before a bag is sold, so what
+          you taste in the cup is as close as possible to what the farmer intended.</p>
+      </div>
+      <button type="button" class="btn" id="summarize-btn">Summarize</button>
+      <div class="journal-summary" id="journal-summary" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></div>
+    </section>
   </main>
 
